,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":548.983394163,"data":"Best Practices:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":548.983395619,"data":"- Use sympy for exact symbolic answers when possible\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":548.983396853,"data":"- Use numpy for numerical verification and large-scale computation\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":548.983398128,"data":"- Combine symbolic and numerical approaches: derive symbolically, verify numerically\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":548.983399498,"data":"- Document your computational strategy clearly\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":548.983400657,"data":"- Validate computational results against known cases or theoretical bounds\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":548.983401944,"data":"- For very large exponents (e.g. a^(n!)), use pow(base, exp, mod) or analytical methods — never materialize the full number\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":548.983403324,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":548.983404514,"data":"# Code Robustness Rules:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":548.983405746,"data":"- Each code cell must be SELF-CONTAINED: re-import and re-define everything you need. If a previous cell errored, its definitions are LOST.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":548.98340713,"data":"- Avoid sympy expressions that grow beyond a few hundred characters. If an expression is exploding, switch to numerical methods (numpy) or modular arithmetic.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":548.983408527,"data":"- For geometry: prefer numpy coordinate models with brute-force verification over pure symbolic or direction-counting approaches.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":548.983409965,"data":"- For combinatorics counting: always verify no duplicates — check injectivity explicitly.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":548.98341125,"data":"- If 5+ code cells without progress, STOP and restart with a different approach.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":548.983413522,"data":"- When using Python, prefer converting sympy expressions to int() before passing to Python builtins like pow(), min(), max().\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":548.983414893,"data":"- Common import: from sympy.ntheory.modular import crt (note: sympy.crt does not exist).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":548.983416206,"data":"- If a code cell fails, re-import necessary libraries in the next cell.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":548.983417469,"data":"- sympy.solve() often times out on complex systems. For polynomial systems with \u003e 3 unknowns, prefer numerical methods (scipy fsolve/minimize) or manual algebraic reduction.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":548.983419221,"data":"- Never call sympy.simplify() or sympy.expand() on expressions involving large binomials or products of many terms. Use float() first to check the numerical value.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":548.983420662,"data":"\n"}
